==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Windy type α''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Divine Windy α''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Ultimate Windy α''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is similar to [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]], except Windy deals [[Massive Damage]] to Floating enemies instead of [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies. Windy is a simple unit, she stays in the back and, if well protected, she will sometimes land a powerful attack that will heavily cripple any Floating enemy caught in the blast, all while dealing acceptable damage to other units. If this sounds familiar, it's due to this unit's many similarities to [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]], who works in the same way.

Despite the potential to deal a lot of damage, Windy has a very inconveniently long attack rate, causing missed hits to hurt so much more and leaving her very vulnerable to being assaulted between an attack and the next, which can, sometimes, even lead her to be knocked back and interrupted multiple times in a row, with little chance to have a comeback. Luckily, Floating enemies often struggle to take advantage of this, making Windy a good match for them. Avoid using units who can [[Knockback|knockback]] Floating, as those Cats make a terrible synergy with Windy.

==='''True Form'''===
Divine Windy α finally receives the stats she needs to keep up with the stronger enemies that can be encountered while progressing in the game, now having a much more usable health and range, which essentially results in Windy having the potential to last twice as long on the field. Her increased damage is a good excuse to bring her along in battles too.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
Ultimate Windy α gets to enjoy improvents to all her noteworthy flaws, and more. Her range increase, while not amazing at first glance, is potentially the most sizeable upgrade over her True Form, setting aside her [[Insane Damage]].

At 510 range, she's capable of outranging almost every common enemy in the game. Including [[Master A.]] and all of his variants, [[THE SLOTH]]/[[Elder Sloth]], [[Calamary]]/[[Cala Maria|Cala Maria]], and even [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]]. Her status as a super backliner further improves her survivability in almost every scenario, allowing her to stay on the field nearly indefinitely. Stacking Windies becomes effortless, since she's typically never in any serious danger; her potential as a generalist nuker goes from just alright, to genuinely incredible.

When it comes to fighting Floating enemies, few can compare to her great power. Just about anything from a simple [[Teacher Bun Bun]] to even [[Mega-Mooth]] can be neutralized with just a few clean shots from her upgraded gear. Her newfound standing range allows her to wipe the floor with [[Gobble]] without ever putting herself into harm's way. There is almost no Floating enemy that stands a chance against her if they don't already outrange her, which is seldom seen in ordinary gameplay as even [[Cli-One]] will fail to stay alive long enough to finish the job.

While [[Pterowl Hazuku]] still poses a major threat to her, Windy's speed should noticeably heighten the chance for her to move in and rip a chunk out of him before being taken to a farm up north.

Overall, a very costly, yet equally rewarding use of your resources.

==='''Talents'''===
Avoid giving her '''[[Freeze]]''', as she will, on average, activate her ability less often than every 26 seconds, which is pathetic, especially for an ability that lasts for 2 seconds. Furthermore, this ability could reset the timer of a longer lasting Freeze effect, which makes unlocking this ability an even worse idea.

'''[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]]''' is recommended, albeit not needed, as it allows her to be used as a complete and reliable counter against [[Othom]], [[Lowkey]], and [[Golem Sunfish]], of which, the first two are exceptionally prevalent in [[Uncanny Legends]]. Additionally, [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Bases]] and [[Loris]] become trivial to deal with. There is no disadvantage to having it, and for such a low NP cost, it should at least be considered for UL.

'''[[Strengthen]]''' brings her damage to new heights; and thanks her exceptional knockback count and health, activating the ability becomes easier than using the unit itself. When active, even non-Floating enemies will take immense damage from her attacks, making her even more useful as a generalist dealing with peons, as well as a specialist evaporating whatever Floating enemies inhabit that same stage.

'''Attack Buff''' and '''HP Buff''' allow her to deal more damage and take more punishment, which synergize well with her Strengthen Talent.

Attack Up and Strengthen are what you should focus on the most, while leaving HP Buff and Curse Immune as a possible bonus to add later. If you are willing to invest in her for real, with both levels and NP, you can even make Windy into your most powerful Floating killer, and a very decent generalist!

==='''Orb'''===
Divine Windy α has Massive Damage, therefore, go with a Floating Massive Damage Orb. Switch to a Defense Up Orb once you unlock her Ultra Form, as her new Insane Damage ability won't be affected by the old Orb. Do NOT switch to an Attack Up Orb as even an S Rank Orb only adds 20,000 damage to Floating.

{{Job|Classification = Nuker & Backliner|UltraClass = Nuker & Super-Backliner}}

