==Trivia==
*She was added to the game alongside [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]] on December 25th, 2013.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Windy, type α was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Cool Breeze, Hot Day (Removed Combo)|Cool Breeze, Hot Day]] and [[Thunder and Lightning (Removed Combo)|Thunder and Lightning]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], Windy's English True and Ultra Forms' names lacked the "α" part.
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Windy's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Windy
A galaxy girl who manipulates wind.
Her vacuum cannon cleans enemies from a distance
Massive damage to Floating enemies. (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Windy, type α
This strange girl can hear the wind whispering.
The wind tells her that it is in pain…
Massive damage to Floating enemies. (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Divine Windy α
Has a bad habit of impulse buying the latest mechas.
Neo-Vacuum Cannon blasts from long-distance.
Massive damage to Floating enemies. (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Ultimate Windy α
Her hair sometimes gets sucked into her mecha.
Fires her Vacuum Cannon Mk 2 from long distance.
Insane damage to Floating enemies. (Area Attack)</pre>
*Windy takes after [[wikipedia:Fūjin|Fujin]] for her theme. The vacuum cleaner that is placed around her back/shoulder is supposed to symbolize Fujin's wind bag. Fujin is also commonly portrayed as a pair with [[wikipedia:Raijin|Raijin]], which is what Thundia is themed after.
*The plugs on Divine Windy α and Ultimate Windy α's "tails" match up perfectly with the outlets on Divine Thundia β and Ultimate Thundia β's.
*Pre-Ultra Form, Windy's attack animation did not match up with her actual attack range, with the point of impact in the animation being further out than the actual attack itself.
*In the original [[Media:075 Concept.JPG|concept art]] for Windy and Thundia, Windy was depicted as having short hair, making her Ultra Form's reduced hair length a return to that first design.
*In the [[Media:Galaxygals img01-03.png|first version]] of the Galaxy Gals' event poster, Windy's favorite thing was said to be her stuffed rabbit named "ウサ夫くん" (Mr. Bunny). This information was omitted from subsequent versions for unknown reasons. However, ウサ夫くん did later appear in an [[Media:0314用風雷 コメント.png|artwork for White Day]] made by PONOS staff.

